e\n\n  * Stored XSS via SVG Files in Content Imports\n\nGHSA-hqq2-xqr2-fmx2 published Oct 1, 2026 by acburdine\n\n  * Stored XSS via Embed Card Previews\n\nGHSA-69qc-f5m6-889c published Oct 1, 2026 by acburdine\n\nHigh\n\n  * Remote Code Execution via Bookmark Card Images\n\nGHSA-788w-68h3-cvxp published Oct 1, 2026 by acburdine\n\n  * Memory Corruption via Crafted Image Uploads\n\nGHSA-cr6m-qrr6-q3j8 published Oct 1, 2026 by acburdine\n\nHigh\n\n  * Private IP Filtering Bypass via IPv6 Transition Addresses\n\nGHSA-r7f2-6fj8-6fg2 published Sep 24, 2026 by acburdine\n\n  * Server-Side Request Forgery in Bookmark Fetching\n\nGHSA-322m-ff4g-9vx9 published Sep 24, 2026 by acburdine\n\nModerate\n\n  * Stored XSS via SVG Uploads Bypassing Sanitization\n\nGHSA-8575-cr6v-7jh4 published Sep 24, 2026 by acburdine\n\n  * Stored XSS via File Uploads on Local Storage\n\nGHSA-gfjp-2p8f-94qv published Sep 17, 2026 by acburdine\n\nHigh\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSymfony Vulnerable to stored XSS in WebProfiler CodeExtension::fileExcerpt() — Unescaped Non-PHP File Rendering · CVE-2026-45072 · GitHub Advisory Database · GitHub (https://github.com/advisories/ghsa-hmr5-2xcr-v8pp)\n【turn240560search6】 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: last week; ## Symfony Vulnerable to stored XSS in WebProfiler CodeExtension::fileExcerpt() — Unescaped Non-PHP File Rendering ...   * https://github.com/FriendsOfPHP/security-advisories/blob/master/symfony/twig-bridge/CVE-2026-45072.yaml\n\n## Symfony Vulnerable to stored XSS in WebProfiler CodeExtension::fileExcerpt() — Unescaped Non-PHP File Rendering\n\nLow severity GitHub Reviewed Published May 20, 2026 in symfony/symfony • Updated May 27, 2026\n\n## Package\n\nsymfony/symfony (Composer)\n\n## Affected versions\n\n>= 6.4.24, < 6.4.40\n\n>= 7.2.9, < 7.4.12\n\n>= 8.0.0, < 8.0.12\n\n## Patched versions\n\n6.4.40\n\n7.4.12\n\n8.0.12\n\nsymfony/twig-bridge (Composer)\n\n>= 6.4.24, < 6.4.40\n\n6.4.40\n\nsymfony/web-profiler-bundle (Composer)\n\n>= 7.2.9, < 7.4.12\n\n>= 8.0.0, < 8.0.12\n\n7.4.12\n\n8.0.12\n\n## Description\n\n### Description\n\nSymfony's profiler, a development only debug UI, renders source-code excerpts on several pages using Twig's custom `file_excerpt` filter. This filter renders PHP files via `highlight_string()` (which escapes HTML), but renders non-PHP files by splitting on `\\n` and interpolating each line directly into `<code>{$line}</code>` with no escaping.\n\nAn attacker who can write arbitrary bytes into any file under the project root (including e.g. `var/log/dev.log`), achieves stored XSS against any developer who later opens that file in the profiler.\n\n### Resolution\n\nThe `file_excerpt` filter now properly escapes each line of non-PHP files using `htmlspecialchars()` before concatenating them.\n\nThe patch for this issue is available here for branch 6.4.\n\n### Credits\n\nSymfony would like to thank Claude Mythos Preview (via Project Glasswing) for reporting the issue and providing the fix.\n\n### References\n\n  * GHSA-hmr5-2xcr-v8pp\n  * symfony/symfony@`863aa81`\n  * https://github.com/FriendsOfPHP/security-advisories/blob/master/symfony/symfony/CVE-2026-45072.yaml\n  * https://github.com/FriendsOfPHP/security-advisories/blob/master/symfony/twig-bridge/CVE-2026-45072.yaml\n  * https://github.com/FriendsOfPHP/security-advisories/blob/master/symfony/web-profiler-bundle/CVE-2026-45072.yaml\n  * https://symfony.com/cve-2026-45072\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity Advisories · TryGhost/Ghost · GitHub (https://github.com/TryGhost/Ghost/security/advisories)\n【turn240560search7】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; ## Security Advisories ...   * Stored XSS via SVG Files in Content Imports ...   * Stored XSS via File Uploads on Local Storage\n\n  1. TryGhost\n  2. Ghost\n\n## Repository navigation\n\n  *   * Code\n  * Issues35 (35)\n  * Pull requests143 (143)\n  